{"body":"## Business Context & Purpose\n\nNode operators and integrators rely on `rad-artifact node status` to understand how much disk space the artifact store is consuming. The `Disk` line in the status output currently always shows `0 B on disk`, making it useless for capacity planning, triggering GC, or monitoring pipelines that parse the JSON output.\n\n- **Who is affected**: anyone running a node and anyone scripting against `--json` output\n- **Impact**: silent misinformation; monitoring dashboards and operators see zero bytes regardless of actual usage\n\n## Current vs. Expected Behavior\n\n**Current output:**\n```\nDisk          0 B on disk · 142.5 MiB logical\n```\n\n**Expected output:**\n```\nDisk          148.3 MiB on disk · 142.5 MiB logical\n```\n\nThe `on disk` figure is intentionally larger than logical: it includes iroh-blobs database overhead, outboard files, and partial downloads. This is correct and expected — the label \"on disk\" is accurate.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- **Empty store**: store directory exists with only iroh metadata; `store_bytes` will be a small nonzero value (correct, not suppressed)\n- **Store path missing**: treat as `0 B` rather than failing the status call\n- **`--reference` imports**: blobs are not copied, so `store_bytes` will undercount logical size — this divergence is expected and the \"on disk\" label remains accurate\n- **Very large stores**: iroh uses a sharded layout; the walk is bounded by file count, not depth\n\n## Research Summary\n\n**Investigation Depth**: STANDARD\n**Confidence Level**: High\n\n### Key Findings\n\n- **Root Cause**: `DiskStats::store_bytes` is hardcoded to `0` in `build_status()` at `src/node/mod.rs:851`. The field is defined and documented correctly in `src/protocol/mod.rs:394` (\"Total bytes on disk under `<home>/artifacts/store/`\"), but the computation is never performed.\n- **Display is correct**: `print_status_pretty` at `src/bin/rad-artifact/node.rs:571` already calls `human_bytes(s.disk.store_bytes)` — it will render correctly once the value is real.\n- **`seeded_bytes_logical` is already correct** — only `store_bytes` needs fixing.\n- **`walkdir` is already a dependency** and used in `src/share/cid_utils.rs:121`.\n- **Store path**: `<home>/artifacts/store/` derived from constants `ARTIFACTS_DIR` + `STORE_DIR` (`src/seeder/mod.rs:62-65`).\n- **Async safety**: the walk is synchronous I/O and should be wrapped in `tokio::task::spawn_blocking` since `build_status` is async.\n- **Effort Estimate**: 2–3 hours\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rad-artifact node status` shows a nonzero `on disk` value after seeding at least one artifact\n- [ ] `status --json` field `disk.store_bytes` equals the measured directory size (not 0)\n- [ ] Missing store directory is handled gracefully (returns 0, does not error)\n- [ ] The directory walk uses `tokio::task::spawn_blocking` to avoid blocking the async runtime\n- [ ] Existing status tests extended to assert `disk.store_bytes > 0` after seeding\n\n## Dependencies & Constraints\n\n- No new dependencies needed (`walkdir` already available)\n- `FsStore` has no total-size API; walk `<home>/artifacts/store/` directly with `walkdir` + `std::fs::metadata`\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n**Key files:**\n- `src/node/mod.rs:851` — `build_status()`, where `store_bytes: 0` needs replacing\n- `src/seeder/mod.rs:62-65` — `ARTIFACTS_DIR`/`STORE_DIR` constants for constructing the path\n- `src/protocol/mod.rs:394` — `DiskStats` struct (no changes needed)\n- `src/bin/rad-artifact/node.rs:571` — display (no changes needed)\n\n**Recommended approach:**\n\nAdd a helper (e.g. in `src/seeder/mod.rs` or `src/node/mod.rs`):\n\n```rust\nasync fn store_size_on_disk(store_path: &Path) -> u64 {\n    let path = store_path.to_owned();\n    tokio::task::spawn_blocking(move || {\n        walkdir::WalkDir::new(&path)\n            .into_iter()\n            .filter_map(|e| e.ok())\n            .filter(|e| e.file_type().is_file())\n            .filter_map(|e| e.metadata().ok())\n            .map(|m| m.len())\n            .sum()\n    })\n    .await\n    .unwrap_or(0)\n}\n```\n\nThen in `build_status()`, replace `store_bytes: 0` with `store_bytes: store_size_on_disk(&store_path).await`.","type":"comment"}